{"author_date": "2024-01-08T20:57:52Z", "author_login": "sajjadazimi", "commit_date": "2024-01-08T20:57:52Z", "committer_login": "web-flow", "message": "kernel tensor approximation (#121)\n\n* kernel tensor approximation fixed: using curve fitting instead of a system of linear equations with polynomial integrals\r\n\r\n* Enabling use of matrix of kernels corresponding to list of distributions instead of a single KernelTensor (makes using Long's kernel possible). Also moving kernels to coal_data and cleaning up functions signitures.\r\n\r\n* add Long's kernel to functions and add a program to test kernel tensor approximations\r\n\r\n* Fix Long kernel example and use a matrix of kernels. Also the polyfit function can now fit in ranges starting from a nonzero value.\r\n\r\n* Add compat entries\r\n\r\n* Add buildkite pipeline\r\n\r\n* debug - make code compatible with the new package version of RecursiveArrayTools\r\n\r\n* Update Project.toml\r\n\r\n* minor debug", "sha": "84edbf783d286abd36bc95174acaed9595928872"}
